-- =============================================================
-- Backfill: restore the state and central schemes that were only
-- ever in the bundled catalogue (src/data/schemes.ts)
--
-- Wiring a real Supabase project into this session today (to fix login)
-- surfaced something worth knowing: `useSchemes()` prefers this live
-- `schemes` table over the bundled fallback whenever it has rows, and this
-- table held exactly ten central schemes and zero state ones. So the
-- Schemes page had been showing FEWER schemes with the real database
-- connected than the bundled fallback alone provided — every state scheme
-- (Bhavantar Bhugtan, Namo Shetkari, KALIA, Rythu Bharosa, Krishak Bandhu,
-- and thirteen more) and sixteen more central schemes had gone invisible.
--
-- This migration is that catalogue's other 32 rows — everything in
-- src/data/schemes.ts not already live and not already covered by
-- 20260908000000_state_farmer_schemes.sql. Generated directly from that
-- file (via esbuild + a small Node script) rather than retyped by hand, so
-- every field matches the bundled data exactly.
--
-- Two ids were deliberately left out, both already present with equivalent
-- content under a different primary key:
--   - 'enam' (bundled) is the same scheme as the live 'e-nam' row. Inserting
--     it would not conflict — different id — and would just duplicate
--     e-NAM under two rows. Left out rather than silently duplicated.
--   - The nine other live ids (kcc, pkvy, pm-kisan, pm-kmy, pm-kusum,
--     pmfby, pmksy, smam, soil-health-card) already match the bundled id
--     exactly, so ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING below already handles them
--     correctly without needing to be excluded by hand.
--
-- ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING: re-running this must not clobber a row an admin
-- has since corrected through the app.
-- =============================================================

ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
